{"agent":"bg61","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":5,"detail":"The new filter only protects `tokenize.COMMENT` and `tokenize.STRING`, but Python 3.12 tokenizes f-string literals as `FSTRING_START`/`FSTRING_MIDDLE`/`FSTRING_END`. Given `ddflow/foo.py` containing `x = f\"subprocess.run('true')\"`, the spawn match sits in an `FSTRING_MIDDLE` token, not a protected `STRING`, so the test records an offender and fails even though the match is purely string text. The converse is also wrong pre-3.12: the whole f-string is emitted as `STRING`, so real spawn code in `f\"{subprocess.run('true')}\"` is suppressed. This filter is therefore incorrect for f-strings under either tokenizer.","digest":"a2ad2e0250c0cec1","family":"deepseek","location":"tests/test_stdio_safety.py:protected","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_stdio_safety.py:protected"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"The new “prose, not a spawn” filter compares `re` offsets to `tokenize` spans, but `generate_tokens` expands tabs to tabsize 8 while `m.start()` is a raw index on the `splitlines()` line. A real call immediately after a same-line string that contains tabs is therefore treated as inside that STRING and dropped. Given `src` containing the valid statement `\"\\t\\t\\t\\t\";subprocess.run([])`, the string token’s expanded end column is 33 while the match starts at raw column 7, so `start <= (n, 7) < end` is true, `offenders` stays empty, and an unguarded spawn passes `test_no_module_spawns_a_process_without_going_through_proc`.","digest":"b049eaf7321fd445","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_stdio_safety.py:174","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_stdio_safety.py:174"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"4/4 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":1,"diff_chars":19439,"diff_sha":"88afc7d334c6cf0f304369a5e55e089850c85f8a937c55f7ef92de7bc3d65af9","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":148.3,"family":"deepseek","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"3a0cab46a4081419","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-main-red-misc-guards.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261108T055518Z-78863580.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4],"reviewed_head":"1bcfc6f35741c26eb6a79dc1efce3f9e87aaafd1","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/services/swarm/lanehooks_check.py":"100644 9391756ef9077d1ef3ad235f90a9484d56c211f9","docs/ddflow/constants-exemptions.d/ddflow.adapters.fsio.toml":"100644 56f48cffd9e1eca1dfcc7ef48f4e99396695f2ba","docs/ddflow/constants-exemptions.d/ddflow.infra.fsio.toml":"100644 af82612fddf300294b02fb33a5b4186a2f60a359","tests/arch_baselines/arch_interfaces.txt":"100644 daf6c582160a3ec2c6c6d4f93159d26b5ee9ebbb","tests/test_arch_deps.py":"100644 5af9fec030059c8899e6af655924190ddb52a08b","tests/test_stdio_safety.py":"100644 41610dd636d0f88acead3213469dd4aa65fe2382","tests/test_write_hook_wire.py":"100644 e2b6bd91d25c77ed6ed57bde4c81c463b25c6103"},"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","reviewer_digest":"dd08c1466c2b8632","reviewer_families":["deepseek","xai"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["tests/test_stdio_safety.py:protected","tests/test_stdio_safety.py:174"],"tree_sha":"1bcfc6f35741+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"e5e17194c4f3c1c4b84351ce7","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":153034,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B-main-red-misc-guards","ts":"2026-11-08T05:57:47.334430Z"}
